What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/1001a000.cpufreq/runtime_state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        X20 board maintainers
Description:
                In addition to the cluster and CCI state, reports
                pm_rails_held, pm_cycles and pm_failures. Before system sleep,
                the driver saves active clusters, clocks and actual manual
                VPROC/VSRAM settings, and temporarily holds each active supply
                at the maximum required by the current manual OPP table.
                Early CPU restoration uses MMIO/secure SRAM accesses only;
                external regulator I2C transfers wait for device resume.
                Original clocks and exact supply settings are then restored.
                pm_rails_held must return to zero after successful recovery.
                A restoration failure retains the held state and increments
                pm_failures; ordinary DVFS/calibration is rejected while held.
                This does not change the OPP table or establish minimum sleep
                power consumption. Counters are reset at driver initialization.
